Since I just had my nose in some of this code...yes:

Higher level monsters are more likely to get a rnd_defensive_item
(also offensive and misc), of which *about* 1/3 are potions of
*healing.  (Many items in the other two categories are also potions,
though their generation functions are even more complex)

Only intelligent non-animal monsters (which don't explode and aren't
type ghost or kop) can get a rnd_defensive_item.  I believe a greater
fraction of monsters are in this group later in the game, though I
haven't tried to confirm this.

(Also, according to pot1-343.txt, there are a lot fewer potions
generated on the ground in Gehennom, but that's not too relevant to
the original discussion.)


